{
 "id": "refund-notified",
 "question": "Who gets notified when a refund is issued?",
 "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
 "recorded": "2026-10-20",
 "answer": "It depends on the refund. There are up to three recipients, and each gets an email only if its condition holds.\n\nThe last step of `shop.refunds.issue_refund` calls `shop.notifications.notify_refund`. That function looks up the customer and emails every recipient that `shop.notifications.refund_recipients` returns:\n\n| Recipient | Condition | Template |\n|---|---|---|\n| The customer (`customer.email`) | Only if `customer.refund_emails` is set (the customer's own setting) | `refund_issued` |\n| Finance (`config.FINANCE_ADDRESS` = `finance@shop.example.test`) | Only if the amount is over `config.FINANCE_REFUND_LIMIT` (250.00) | `refund_finance` |\n| Support (`config.SUPPORT_ADDRESS` = `support@shop.example.test`) | Only if `reason == \"fraud\"` | `refund_fraud` |\n\nIf none of the conditions hold, nobody is notified. Each email goes through `shop.notifications.send_email`, which records an `email.sent` event in the log.\n\nSource: the `shop.refunds`, `shop.notifications` and `shop.config` modules.",
